"abstract":"<title>Abstract</title>
                <p>Vision-language models (VLMs) have demonstrated strong zero-shot learning (ZSL) capability in open-category recognition through joint image-text modeling. However, existing approaches for improving zero-shot performance often rely on large-scale pretraining, prompt learning, or lightweight adaptation, which involve high training costs, strong task dependence, or insufficient optimization of the shared representation space. In particular, during post-pretraining, the modality gap, distributional degradation, and representation collapse may emerge simultaneously, limiting further improvements in zero-shot classification performance.

To address these issues, this paper proposes GeoRel-CLIP, a geometry-regularized relational distillation method for CLIP post-pretraining. Instead of solely reducing the distance between image and text features, GeoRel-CLIP jointly optimizes the shared embedding space from two perspectives: global geometric distribution and local relational structure . Specifically, we introduce a Geometric Distribution Regularization (GDR) module to regulate feature spreading and directional occupancy balance on the unit hypersphere, thereby suppressing excessive feature aggregation and representation collapse. Meanwhile, we further propose a Scale-Invariant Relational Distillation (SIRD) module, which standardizes and aligns the cross-modal relational matrices of the teacher and student models, reducing the interference caused by scale drift and enhancing the consistency of structural knowledge transfer. Experimental results show that GeoRel-CLIP outperforms existing SOTA methods on multiple standard zero-shot datasets and achieves further improvement in the average Top-1 accuracy across 11 datasets.</p>","DOI":"10.21203/rs.3.rs-9878849/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,3]],"date-time":"2026-08-03T08:19:13Z","timestamp":1785745153000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["GeoRel-CLIP: Boosting CLIP Zero-Shot Recognition via Geometry-Regularized Relational Distillation"],"prefix":"10.21203","author":[{"given":"Huadong","family":"Sun","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Harbin University of Commerce"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yexuan","family":"Zhao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Harbin University of Commerce"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Junwei","family":"Tong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Harbin University of Commerce"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"297","link":[{"URL":"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-9878849/v1","content-type":"text/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-9878849/v1.html","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,3]],"date-time":"2026-08-03T08:19:13Z","timestamp":1785745153000},"score":22.738132,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-9878849/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,3]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-9878849/v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,3]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,5]],"date-time":"2022-04-05T10:12:55Z","timestamp":1649153575051},"reference-count":27,"publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2011,2,25]],"date-time":"2011-02-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1298592000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":7360,"URL":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["MRS Proc."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1991]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT</jats:title><jats:p>The properties of electric double layers near curved surfaces of arbitrary shape and genus are obtained exactly within the Debye-Hückel theory by means of <jats:italic>multiple-scattering expansion</jats:italic>. For smooth membranes, geometric and topological feature of the electrostatic free energy then emerge through convergent expansions in inverse powers of the principal radii of curvature. Some consequences for the electrostatic stability of various membrane shapes are considered. We also study the effects of surface singularities, e.g., wedges, on the thermodynamics of electric double layers near a rough colloid. Each wedge yields an additive contribution to the free energy <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="S1946427400459002_inline1" /> that is a functionof the angle. A probabilistic Brownian representation of <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="S1946427400459002_inline1" /> is given, which is entirely similar to that of vibration eigenmodes given by M. Kac long ago in <jats:italic>“Canone hear the shape of a drum?”</jats:italic> [Amer. Math. Monthly 73S, 1 (1966)]. The analysis yields a universal scaling law for the free energy of a rough colloid with its fractal Minkowski dimension.</jats:p>","DOI":"10.1557/proc-253-441","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2011,3,6]],"date-time":"2011-03-06T05:33:19Z","timestamp":1299389599000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Complex Geometry and Electric Double Layers"],"prefix":"10.1557","volume":"253","author":[{"given":"Bertrand","family":"Duplantier","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"297","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,2,25]]},"reference":[{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref027","first-page":"1497","volume-title":"C.R. Acad. Sci.","volume":"307","author":"Brochard-Wyart","year":"1988"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref024","first-page":"4525","volume":"A43","author":"Bensimon","year":"1991","journal-title":"Phys. Rev."},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref023","volume-title":"Total Curvature in Riemannian Geometry","author":"Willmore","year":"1982"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref022","volume-title":"Nova Science","author":"Duplantier","year":"1991"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref021","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/0021-9797(69)90401-9"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref020","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103/PhysRevLett.67.2974"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref019","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007/BF01210795"},{"key":"S1946427400459002_ref015","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DO